DERIVED WORK — ARM optimized-routines
================================================================================

`src/fast_exp.rs`, `src/fast_log.rs` and `src/fast_pow.rs` are Rust
transcriptions of ARM optimized-routines' `math/exp.c` + `math/exp_data.c`,
`math/log.c` + `math/log_data.c`, and `math/pow.c` + `math/pow_common.h` +
`math/pow_log_data.c` respectively. This is the implementation **glibc itself
ships** for these three functions (ARM contributed it upstream), which is why
the ports are both fast and, modulo one compiler contraction, bit-compatible
with the platform libm on Linux.

