DERIVED WORK — faer (dense SVD), faer-traits and pulp
================================================================================

`src/faer_dense/` ports the path faer 0.24.4's `Mat::svd()` runs for a small
square f64 matrix: Householder bidiagonalisation (`svd/bidiag.rs`), the
bidiagonal QR algorithm (`svd/bidiag_svd.rs`), the block-size-1 reflector
application (`householder.rs`), the dot / matvec / norm / Givens kernels, the
scalar `hypot` of faer-traits 0.24.0, and a scalar model of pulp 0.22.3's V3
(AVX2+FMA) lane semantics that faer's SIMD kernels run on. Ported 2026-10-20
at the maintainer's direction (gh #996: "Whatever faer does, port into
petir"), so that `outram-blender` could drop faer. The full MIT notice is
reproduced in every file header.

